## Step-by-Step Triage & Mitigation

### Step 1 — Inspect System Telemetry

Check current error rates and active container pods:

```bash
kubectl get pods -n <namespace> -l app=<service-name>
kubectl logs -n <namespace> -l app=<service-name> --tail=100 -f
```

### Step 2 — Execute Mitigation Action

```bash
# Set placeholder variables
export SERVICE_NAME="<SERVICE_NAME>"
export NEW_SECRET="<NEW_SECRET_VALUE>"

# Run the remediation command
kubectl rollout restart deployment/<SERVICE_NAME> -n <namespace>
```

### Step 3 — Verify Recovery

Check that the deployment achieves ready status and error rates drop:

```bash
kubectl rollout status deployment/<SERVICE_NAME> -n <namespace>
curl -f https://<service>.internal/healthz
```

---

## Rollback Plan

If the mitigation fails or symptoms worsen:

```bash
kubectl rollout undo deployment/<SERVICE_NAME> -n <namespace>
```

## Post-Incident Actions

1. Post an update in `#incidents` confirming resolution.
2. File a follow-up ticket in the team board for root-cause analysis.
3. If this was a Sev1/Sev2 incident, draft an [Incident Postmortem](../postmortems/<DATE>-<INCIDENT_SLUG>.md).
